  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 216 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nAnother quiet afternoon across the area, with light southeasterly \nwinds and clear skies in the vicinity of surface ridging. The core \nof the mid-level jet remains to our north, with above normal 500 mb \nheights dominating the majority of the CONUS. This tranquil pattern \nwill remain in place for several more days. Several weak waves to \nour north and northeast will push a few weak fronts/wind shifts \nthrough, but with the continued upper ridging we'll see warm \ntemperatures persisting. Expecting continued highs in the upper 70s \nto mid 80s with lows in the 50s to low 60s. Given limited moisture \nand the presence of synoptic subsidence for much of the time, dry \nconditions are expected through Sunday. The one possible exception \nmay be Thursday into Friday as a weak boundary sets up across far \nnorthern KS, but even then any rainfall amounts would be light.\n\nBy the very end of the period early next week (or just beyond), \nthere are some signs of change. Good agreement in long range \nguidance for a deep upper low developing over the western CONUS \nbefore shifting eastward to the Plains. But timing, amplitude, \ntiming of individual shortwaves, etc are yet to be determined this \nfar out.",
